From: rnsbox <rnsbox@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: sophgo: module-01-evb: USB gadget mode and uart1

The RNSBox portal exposes a CDC-NCM management interface on the board's
single USB-C port, so the DWC2 controller must run in peripheral mode
(the SoC dtsi defaults it to host). UART1 is the HaLow SLIP line
(S31slip muxes XGPIOA[28]/[29] at boot); the SoC dtsi leaves it
disabled, so no /dev/ttyS1 appears without this.

Unlike the Duo S port there is no disppll/cam0_200 reclock here: the
UART stays at its 1,562,500 ceiling and slip.conf ships 1.5 Mbaud (same
reasoning as the Duo S arm64 patch).

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duo-module-01-evb.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duo-module-01-evb.dts
index 9fa77ba..b5d43ab 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duo-module-01-evb.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duo-module-01-evb.dts
@@ -72,5 +72,14 @@
 	disable-wp;
 	pinctrl-0 = <&sdhci0_cfg>;
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+&usb {
+	dr_mode = "peripheral";
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&uart1 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
-- 
